174
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
So, as you heard last week

175
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
and when we were talking in the mailbag here,

176
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
I've been having an ongoing conversation

177
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:20,000
with a buddy down in Virginia, James Chaplin,

178
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
about their High Adventure plans.

179
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
I want to take a moment to encourage you

180
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
to get your own High Adventure program off the ground

181
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Now. usually when we're talking High Adventure,

182
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:33,000
we capitalize the H

183
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
and we capitalize the A

184
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:38,000
and we think of the BSA's most popular

185
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
and heavily promoted Big Three High Adventure bases:

186
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
Fillmont, the Florida Sea Base

187
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
and Northern Tier up in Minnesota.

188
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
Council-level High Adventure programs

189
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
usually focus on putting crews together

190
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
for trips to those three destinations,

191
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
And there's a lot of council-level

192
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
High Adventure experiences out there.

193
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
But I want to tell you something:

194
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
there are hundreds, if not thousands,

195
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
of other places for Scouts to experience

196
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:05,000
a High Adventure trip.

197
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
with a little ingenuity, a little planning

198
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
and a little vision,

199
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Every Scout should be able to participate

200
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
in some kind of High Adventure trip

201
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
at least once while he's a Boy Scout.

202
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
I want to challenge you here

203
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
to stretch your understanding

204
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
of what High Adventure is

205
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
and to go beyond your comfort zone

206
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
and to ultimately make it happen

207
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
for your Scouts.

208
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
So the first myth we wanted to spell

209
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
is: High Adventure trips

210
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
don't have to happen at a High Adventure base

211
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
or as a part of a

212
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:40,000
quote- official, unquote- program.

213
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
You can put together your own High Adventure trip.

214
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
You really really can.

215
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
It can happen anywhere.

216
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
There are state and national parks

217
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
in the country

218
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,000
that offer great places for hiking

219
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
and backpacking, climbing, canoeing

220
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
and kayaking.

221
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,000
You don't have to travel far

222
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
or go to exotic locations,

223
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
and that's another myth.

224
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:05,000
High Adventure only happens

225
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
in these distant, exotic places.

226
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
No, no,

227
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
High Adventure is not a place,

228
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
It's a state of mind,

229
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
A challenge beyond our normal weekend camping trips.

230
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
High Adventure is about

231
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
doing more than where you go.

232
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
Fillman is a great location,

233
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
but it's not High Adventure

234
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
without the right mindset

235
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
and the right participants.

236
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
Four or five days of backpacking

237
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
a couple hours drive from home,

238
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
rather than getting on a plane

239
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
and flying to some exotic location,

240
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
can be as exciting, adventurous

241
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,000
and rewarding as any trip.

242
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
The most important location

243
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
for High Adventure begins between your two ears.

244
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
It's your attitude.

245
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,000
That's what makes it High Adventure.

246
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,000
The next myth we wanted to spell

247
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
is: to lead a High Adventure trip,

248
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
you have to be a highly trained

249
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
High Adventure expert.

250
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Well, you do not have to be

251
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
an expert to lead a High Adventure trip,

252
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
and I can tell you this

253
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
authoritatively because I'm no expert

254
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
and I've led plenty of them.

255
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
You'll need some important training:

256
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
weather and safety

257
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
and first aid training- all very important.

258
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
You'll also need to plan your trip

259
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,000
to be slightly below your estimated

260
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
skill level,

261
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
and your High Adventure does not need

262
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
to be dangerous

263
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
to be challenging.

264
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Rely on the experience that others have had

265
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,000
and educate yourself about these things.

266
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
read books and practice your skills

267
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
and you're going to be plenty

268
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
expert enough to pull off a High Adventure trip.

269
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:35,000
Remember that

270
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
our scouting organization

